<title>POLAND: Kredyt Bank gets PLN 60 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Kredyt Bank gets PLN 60 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Large Polish state-owned bank PKO BP has granted Kredyt Bank SA credit worth 60 million zlotys for a period of 42 months, Kredyt Bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The statement said the interest would be based on the six-month WIBOR rate increased by 65 basis points.</p>
<p>Kredyt has said it seeks about 100 million zlotys in subordinated loans to effect its planned merger with Polish Investment Bank (PBI), which could be completed by year-end.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
